# Copy to .env.local

# Postgres database URL and settings.
# Default is a local Docker Compose setup.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://ratel:ratel@localhost:5432/ratel
DATABASE_MIGRATE_ON_BOOT=1

# Where SDK snippets in the console point: this deployment's origin.
# The console adds /api/v1 when it builds API and ingest URLs.
BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Experimental features, all off by default: the eval gate (test a fix on the project's past
# runs before it ships), session replay with the session chat, the Traces Sessions tab, the
# Health score and the early readings, the redesigned trace views, raw OTLP capture (each
# accepted request body kept, gzipped, up to OTLP_RAW_DAILY_BYTES per project per day),
# adaptive labelling, the MCP server's interactive views (MCP Apps), tool-run insights and the
# removal of senders' IP addresses at ingest. 1 turns them all on.
# RATEL_EXPERIMENTAL_FEATURES=1
# The eval gate's models: re-rank fixes simulate in process. Fixes that need a model replay,
# and judged criteria, call Anthropic with ANTHROPIC_API_KEY; without it they say no model is
# configured and nothing calls out. EVAL_GATE_MOCK_MODEL=1 uses deterministic stand-ins instead
# (ignored when APP_ENV is production).
# EVAL_GATE_MOCK_MODEL=1
# EVAL_GATE_REPLAY_BUDGET_USD=1
# EVAL_GATE_JUDGE_BUDGET_USD=0.1
# Advanced: FF_EVAL_GATE alone turns on the eval gate (run_eval and get_eval need it too).
# FF_RANKING_CATALOG_DRIFT alone turns on adaptive ranking's catalog drift: a tool is gone only when a
# published catalog dropped it and it went unused past a grace period; warnings are closable, and
# gone tools are pruned from the graph on rebuild.
# FF_MCP_APPS alone turns on MCP Apps: the MCP server publishes interactive ui:// views (built by
# pnpm mcp-apps:build) and points its tools at them, for hosts that show views.
# FF_TOOL_RUN_INSIGHTS alone turns on tool-run insights: tasks mined from a floor of three runs, a
# derived ask for a tool-only run, an OTel invoke_agent root span as an agent run with its own turn
# and task, and an Agent health reading from 10 turns marked low confidence.
# FF_TYPED_STEPS alone turns on typed steps: OTel model calls, code steps, handoffs and user messages
# are turn steps, so a trace with model calls only makes a turn and reaches Agent health.
# FF_SANDBOXES alone turns on agent sandboxes: the Sandboxes pages and run API, `ratel sandbox dev`
# runners (POST /api/v1/runner/connect, through packages/gateway), the sandbox stamps on the
# label and topic jobs, and playground runs kept out of cost and Agent health.
# FF_PIVOTS alone turns on pivots: Settings > Pivots, the configured pivot keys kept on span rows
# at ingest, and `dims` (each pivot's value) on trace summaries, refilled when a pivot changes.
# FF_CUSTOM_DASHBOARDS alone turns on custom dashboards: the Dashboards pages under Overview
# (widgets over trace summaries, shared with the project by link) and the MCP tools
# list_dashboards and get_dashboard.
# FF_CODE_HANDOFF alone turns on code handoff: Settings > Repository links a project to a GitHub
# repo through your own GitHub App (the GITHUB_APP_* variables below) and its webhook,
# POST /api/github/webhook.
# FF_VARIANT_EXPERIMENTS alone turns on variant experiments: OTLP ingest keeps each span's
# ratel.variant.* tags (or a project's own attribute mapped in Settings > General) and the summary
# sweep rolls them up per trace; the Variants pages under Traces and the MCP tools
# list_variant_experiments and get_variant_experiment compare the variants of an experiment.
# FF_FINE_TUNING alone turns on fine-tuning: the Fine-tuning page under Improvements (a project's
# training opt-in, use cases over its model calls and their stats, redacted dataset versions built
# by the build_fine_tuning_dataset job), its API routes and the MCP tools list_use_cases,
# get_use_case, create_use_case, build_dataset and get_dataset. FINE_TUNING_MAX_DATASET_ROWS caps
# the rows of one dataset version (default 50000; over it the build fails with too_large).
# FF_INGEST_STRIP_CLIENT_ADDRESS alone makes OTLP ingest remove the sender's IP address attributes
# (host.ip, client.address, forwarding headers, ...) before decode and raw capture. An MCP caller's
# country is still read from the removed address first; the address itself is never stored.
# Everything else is on for every deployment, as upstream retired its flags: session replay (a
# session as a chat, and What-if), the v3 trace views, raw OTLP capture, Traces Sessions, adaptive
# labelling, the Health score and the quick and import first readings.
# Raw OTLP request bodies: stored gzipped bytes one project may add per UTC day (default 1 GiB,
# 0 stores none), and their retention, which applies even with DATA_RETENTION_ENABLED unset
# (500 rows per tick).
# OTLP_RAW_DAILY_BYTES=1073741824
# OTLP_RAW_RETENTION_DAYS=30
# Client geo (RC-774): the DB-IP IP-to-Country Lite mmdb file that gives an MCP caller's IP its
# country. Ingest reads the country, then drops the IP: no table keeps it. The image ships the file
# (src/Dockerfile); for a bare `pnpm dev`, get it with `node src/scripts/fetch-geo-db.mjs <path>`.
# Unset or unreadable, countries stay null (one log line). Data under CC BY 4.0: IP Geolocation by
# DB-IP (https://db-ip.com).
# GEO_COUNTRY_MMDB_PATH=/absolute/path/dbip-country-lite.mmdb

# Where Claude calls go. Unset, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY selects the Anthropic API.
# bedrock = every Claude call goes to Amazon Bedrock through eu.* inference
# profiles, signed by the AWS credential chain; ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is never used.
# AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK turns Claude off (it would replace the AWS credential
# chain); ANTHROPIC_BEDROCK_BASE_URL is ignored. Any other value turns Claude off.
# ANTHROPIC_BACKEND=bedrock

# Self-telemetry: the platform's own traces and logs, over OTLP/HTTP. Off unless both
# endpoints are set; with either one unset nothing is exported and nothing leaves the
# process. The _HEADERS variables carry the collector's credentials ("key=value,key=value").
# OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG is the share of traces kept (0 to 1, default 1) and
# OTEL_SDK_DISABLED=true turns it all off. Buffered telemetry is flushed on SIGTERM; outside
# the worker that needs NEXT_MANUAL_SIG_HANDLE=true, or Next may exit before the flush ends.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318/v1/traces
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_LOGS_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318/v1/logs
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_HEADERS=
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_LOGS_HEADERS=
# OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG=1
# The service name these traces and logs carry (the OpenTelemetry standard variable).
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=ratel-platform
# Server traces for APM: requests, Postgres queries and outbound calls, over OTLP/HTTP to a
# collector of your own (an OpenTelemetry Collector, a Datadog Agent…). Off unless the base
# endpoint is set; traces go to its /v1/traces. Independent of self-telemetry. Never sent:
# model-call and MCP tool spans, and URL query strings. SERVER_TRACES_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES
# ("key=value,…") overrides this exporter's resource, e.g. service.name and service.version.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=
# SERVER_TRACES_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES=service.name=ratel-platform
# Ratel as a customer of itself, riding on the self-telemetry above. With a project key and
# that deployment's /v1/traces (no default destination), the model calls Ratel pays for go to
# the key's project as gen_ai spans, with their prompt and answer; each background job that
# calls a model is one agent run there (invoke_agent <job kind>, with the job's ask). A second
# key sends each call to Ratel's own MCP tools, as an execute_tool span with its arguments and
# result, to a project of its own. Both hold customers' data. REPLACE_ME counts as unset.
# RATEL_SELF_TELEMETRY_ENDPOINT=
# RATEL_SELF_TELEMETRY_API_KEY=
# RATEL_SELF_TELEMETRY_PROJECT_ID=
# RATEL_SELF_TELEMETRY_MCP_API_KEY=

# Sandbox playground (FF_SANDBOXES): where `ratel sandbox dev` runners connect, and the HMAC key
# shared with the gateway (packages/gateway). Both are needed for POST /api/v1/runner/connect.
# SANDBOX_GATEWAY_URL=ws://localhost:8787
# SANDBOX_GATEWAY_TOKEN_SECRET=

# GitHub App (code handoff, FF_CODE_HANDOFF). Optional: without all six the Repository tab says
# "not configured" and the webhook answers 503. Self-hosters register their own App: GitHub >
# Settings > Developer settings > GitHub Apps > New GitHub App. Set the webhook URL to
# <BASE_URL>/api/github/webhook with a webhook secret, turn on "Request user authorization (OAuth)
# during installation" and set the callback URL to <BASE_URL>/api/github/setup. The App needs
# repository Metadata (read), Contents (read: the code index searches and reads files) and Issues
# (write: a handoff opens an issue for Claude Code), and the installation, push and deployment
# status events (the deploy watch records fix-tagged commits and when they go live). The private key is the PEM (newlines as
# \n is fine). Never commit the values.
GITHUB_APP_ID=
GITHUB_APP_SLUG=
GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=
GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_SECRET=
